-- Q13794: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under FRCP Rule 26(b)(3) and IRC Section 7525, the work product doctrine provides two tiers of protection. Ordinary work product such as factual compilations may be discovered upon showing substantial need and undue hardship. Opinion work product including mental impressions and legal theories receives nearly absolute protection.
Wrong (A): The doctrine distinguishes between ordinary and opinion work product, providing different levels of protection rather than the same level for each.
Wrong (C): The protection levels are reversed; factual compilations receive the lower tier of protection, not absolute protection, while the memorandum receives near-absolute protection.
Wrong (D): CPAs may invoke the work product doctrine when materials are prepared in anticipation of litigation; the protection is not limited to attorneys.$EXPL$
