-- Q13823: Government Regulation of Business [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 8.01, the duty of loyalty is the fiduciary obligation requiring an agent to act in the principal''s best interest and refrain from self-dealing and conflicts of interest. It is the most fundamental fiduciary duty in an agency relationship.
Wrong (A): The duty of care under Section 8.08 requires reasonable competence and diligence but does not specifically address self-dealing or conflicts of interest.
Wrong (B): The duty of obedience requires the agent to follow the principal''s lawful instructions, not to avoid conflicts of interest.
Wrong (C): The duty to notify requires the agent to inform the principal of material information, not to refrain from self-dealing.$EXPL$
