UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 1.01, an agency relationship requires only mutual consent between principal and agent. No consideration, written agreement, or state filing is necessary, and a gratuitous agency is legally valid.
Wrong (A): Compensation is not required; a gratuitous agency where the agent acts without payment is fully valid under common law.
Wrong (B): A written agreement is generally not required for agency formation; oral agreements and implied conduct suffice unless the equal dignities doctrine applies.
