-- Q13828: Government Regulation of Business [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Restatement (Third) of Agency Section 3.12, an agency coupled with an interest exists when the agent holds a security interest in the subject matter, making the agency irrevocable. Monroe''s security interest in Prescott''s inventory survives both the attempted revocation and Prescott''s subsequent incapacity.
Wrong (B): Principals do not have an absolute right to revoke all agencies; an agency coupled with an interest is an exception because the agent''s own property rights are at stake.
Wrong (C): An agency coupled with an interest survives both revocation and incapacity, not just one of the two events.
Wrong (D): Not all agencies terminate upon incapacity; an agency coupled with an interest is specifically designed to survive such events by operation of law.$EXPL$
